<title>INDIA: India revises 95/96 GDP growth down at 6.6 pct.</title>
<headline>India revises 95/96 GDP growth down at 6.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government said on Friday that the revised growth rate of gross domestic product (GDP) for 1995/96 (April-March) was 6.6 percent, down from an earlier estimate of 7.0 percent.  </p>
<p>The previous estimate had been released in July.</p>
<p>The government said in a statement that the latest estimates incorporated more up-to-date data relating to agricultural and industrial production.</p>
<p>Newspapers had recently said that the 1995/96 GDP growth rate had been revised downward to 6.3 percent.</p>
<p>Following are revised estimates of GDP at factor cost by kind of economic activity for 1995/96 at 1980/81 prices:</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    INDUSTRY		 PERCENTAGE CHANGE OVER PREVIOUS YEAR</p>
<p>					    1994/95	   1995/96</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Agriculture, forestry, fishing	4.9		 0.9</p>
<p>Mining and quarrying		    4.3		 5.0</p>
<p>Manufacturing			     9.0		13.5</p>
<p>Electricity, gas, water supply	8.0		 8.3</p>
<p>Construction				7.1		 4.7</p>
<p>Trade, hotels, transport,</p>
<p> communication			    8.0		10.1</p>
<p>Financing, insurance, real</p>
<p> estate, business services	    4.3		 5.6</p>
<p>Community, social, personal</p>
<p> services				   4.3		 4.1</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Total GDP at factor cost		6.3		 6.6</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
